WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:00.660
Here it is!

00:00:02.020 --> 00:00:03.220
This little building

00:00:03.220 --> 00:00:06.300
is a $2 million dollar bathroom

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:07.680
$2 million dollars?

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:09.180
I had to check it out.

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:12.820
I was expecting gold plated fixtures.

00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:16.700
It's just a toilet, a couple urinals, 2 sinks.

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:17.880
$2 million dollars?

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:21.960
Do the people who use the park know what

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:24.300
taxpayers paid for their bathroom?

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:25.720
What do you think this cost?

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:27.500
A couple thousand.

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:29.120
$70,000?

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:31.660
Approximately $100,000 maybe

00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:34.880
They spent $2 million dollars

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:36.180
For this?

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:37.340
Unbelievable.

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:38.320
Wow

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:39.540
Wow

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:41.880
You could buy a nice house here for $2 million dollars.

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:43.540
For that price, yeah, you could buy a big house here

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:44.300
You can!

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:46.180
This nearby house was advertised

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:47.960
for much less.

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:49.620
It has 6 bedrooms!

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:51.080
In the millions, for this?

00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:52.260
This is ridiculous.

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:53.460
Where’s the money go?

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:54.460
Good question.

00:00:54.460 --> 00:00:56.460
Everything costs more

00:00:56.460 --> 00:00:57.840
when government builds it.

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:00.540
Washington, D.C.'s Visitor Center was supposed to cost

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:02.260
$265 million,

00:01:02.260 --> 00:01:05.240
it ended up costing $621 million.

00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:07.020
The Veterans Affairs medical center

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:11.020
near Denver was projected to cost $590 million.

00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:13.800
Now they estimate $1.7 billion.

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:16.100
Government spends more

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:19.240
because every decision is tied up in endless rules.

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:20.800
Minority outreach.

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:22.520
Wheelchair access.

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:23.700
Zoning rules.

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:24.800
And much more.

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:26.740
Your department puts out a statement

00:01:26.740 --> 00:01:29.500
current estimate to build a new bathroom

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:31.860
is 3 million dollars

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:33.920
It is now approaching in some cases

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:35.680
going over 3 million.

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:38.340
Mitchell Silver is New York's Parks Commissioner.

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:40.100
This is the most expensive market

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:40.980
in the world.

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:42.880
So $2 million was a good deal here?

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:43.880
$2million was a good deal.

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:47.040
We built these comfort stations to last.

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:50.120
But you can buy whole houses

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:51.240
in that neighborhood

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:53.680
for less than what you spent on this bathroom

00:01:54.760 --> 00:01:56.320
I hear that point often

00:01:56.320 --> 00:01:58.560
and If you look at the material we use

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:00.160
compared to a home

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:02.800
these are very, very durable material.

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:04.060
That’s nice.

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:07.000
But this bathroom is made of durable materials too.

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:08.220
It’s so beautiful

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:11.420
that a newspaper&nbsp;said it might be the fanciest in New York.

00:02:11.420 --> 00:02:12.520
Yet it cost

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:14.580
one fifth as much as much.

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:15.540
Why?

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:17.660
Well, it's in nearby Bryant Park,

00:02:17.660 --> 00:02:20.260
and Bryant Park is privately managed.

00:02:20.260 --> 00:02:22.480
Bryant Park built one

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:25.700
with just as many sinks and toilets for

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:27.840
a fifth the price

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:29.640
Bryant Park did a renovation.

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:31.040
When we build our comfort stations

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:33.060
we do it from the ground up.

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:34.260
But why?

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:35.460
Why’d they knock down the old one down?

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:36.840
It just looks like the same thing.

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:39.560
Commissioner Silver says this has to be especially

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:40.840
sturdy, because...

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:42.240
We’re going to expect

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:44.240
thousands, if not hundreds of thousands,

00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:45.000
of visitors

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:45.980
in that facility

00:02:45.980 --> 00:02:47.660
over its life cycle.

00:02:47.660 --> 00:02:50.520
But privately run Bryant Park gets&nbsp;more use.

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:52.020
No comparison.

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:54.400
It's so busy people wait in line to get in.

00:02:55.160 --> 00:02:57.780
Yet another reason government work costs more

00:02:57.780 --> 00:02:59.980
is that government pays more.

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:01.800
We pay prevailing wage.

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:03.040
Prevailing wage?

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:04.400
Prevailing wage.

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:05.340
Union wage.

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:07.920
This is a city that does believe strongly in labor

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:09.020
and they want to make sure that people

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:10.340
get paid prevailing wage.

00:03:10.340 --> 00:03:13.500
Prevailing wage turns out to mean union wages.

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:15.900
Sometimes more than 100 dollars an hour.

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:18.240
That makes everything cost more.

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:19.540
And when we watched

00:03:19.540 --> 00:03:21.840
the workers didn’t seem to work very hard.

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:23.900
The final reason this so much

00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:25.900
is that it took years to build it.

00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:26.920
It took less time

00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:28.720
to build the Empire state building.

00:03:29.380 --> 00:03:31.600
We’ve now saved 5 months

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:33.040
out of what used to be

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:34.920
4 years, 5 years for a project.

00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:37.980
now doing them 3 years, in some cases under.

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:39.460
So we shaved 5 years off.

00:03:39.460 --> 00:03:42.980
Whoop dee do. So it’s 5 years, 4 ½ years?

00:03:42.980 --> 00:03:44.360
That’s still terrible

00:03:44.360 --> 00:03:46.140
We’re actually 3 years and now we just finished

00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:48.340
one of our projects in under 3 years.

00:03:48.340 --> 00:03:51.040
Why does it take you 3 years to build a bathroom?

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:54.060
We have a process that includes design,

00:03:54.060 --> 00:03:55.320
procurement

00:03:55.320 --> 00:03:55.960
and construction.

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:57.940
But so does the private sector

00:03:57.940 --> 00:04:00.060
Ours because it’s a public project

00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:02.420
we believe very strongly in engaging the public,

00:04:02.420 --> 00:04:04.760
“Engaging the public” means things like
the

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:06.400
city planning department’s

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:09.540
“uniform land use review procedure."

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:11.180
Try doing something quickly

00:04:11.180 --> 00:04:12.920
while following these rules.

00:04:12.920 --> 00:04:15.440
Clearly the private sector does not have to go through the same process.

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:17.380
And this is a good thing, the public process?

00:04:17.380 --> 00:04:18.080
All these meetings?

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:19.780
Oh yes it’s a good thing.

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:21.980
That's a ridiculous amount of money.

00:04:21.980 --> 00:04:23.700
One little building

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:25.240
$2 million dollars

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:27.120
That’s government at work.

